with different monsters appearing as the same symbol in nh3 the "/",
look, key becomes a significant feature and should be single purpose,
(i.e. always specify by cursor). that functionality could get expanded
so that, for example, you don't have to use 7 "/"'s to see 7 monsters.
the expanded functionality would provide a list of monsters seen
(see-able) along the path that you specified while moving the cursor.
in its simplest form if you move the cursor over a given monster more
than once then it will show up in the list as many times as you moved
the cursor over it. the first entry in the list would be the first
monster that you moved the cursor over, and so on.
the specify by symbol function belongs under the "?", help, key
features.

an additional feature that i'd like is "filtered" discoveries. when you
use the "\", discover, key it could ask for [!=?/a] as an example,
using whatever is appropriate at the time and where a=all as it is now
and ! would only show potions, etc.

